Algorithmic basis
-----------------
The polycistronic tRNA-gRNA (PTG) design procedure implements and extends the
approach established in the first version of this tool:

  [AUTHORS]. [TITLE]. International Journal of Biological Macromolecules
  [VOLUME], [PAGES] ([YEAR]).
  https://doi.org/[DOI]

Version 2.0 extends that work with support for up to 12 spacers, 12 Type IIS
restriction enzymes, selectable native (76 nt) and engineered (86 nt) gRNA
scaffolds, configurable Cas9 plasmid vector overhangs, and internal recognition
site detection.


